    "description": "Asti Corporation engages in the manufacture and sale of electrical equipment for cars in Japan. The company offers automotive electrical components, including air conditioner panels, car radios, BCM PCB, vehicle controllers, plastic molded products and corner sensors for four wheeled vehicles; grip heaters, power tuner, charger, DC/DC convertor, invertor, pilot lamps for two wheeled vehicles; and controllers and switch boxes for electric vehicles. It also provides home and industrial electronics, such as display and electric control boards for automatic washing machines, and dishwashers; controllers for industrial robots; and rice and wheat dryer controllers. In addition, the company offers wire harnesses for boats, two-wheeled and four-wheeled vehicles, and racing cars. Further, it provides power electronic products comprising e-mobility power boards for chargers and e-mobility DC/DC converters, as well as medical devices. The company was formerly known as Taiheiyou ASTI Corp. and changed its name to Asti Corporation in January 1992. Asti Corporation was incorporated in 1963 and is headquartered in Hamamatsu, Japan."
